---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const contents = [
  ['summary', 'Summary'],
  ['owner', 'Who is responsible'],
  ['hosting', 'Hosting and server logs'],
  ['cookies', 'Cookies and local storage'],
  ['email', 'If you email me'],
  ['links', 'External links'],
  ['rights', 'Your rights'],
  ['content', 'Content and copyright'],
  ['changes', 'Changes'],
] as const;
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy notice for akaminas.github.io: a static site with no cookies, no analytics and no tracking. What the hosting provider (GitHub Pages) logs, what happens when you email me, and your rights."
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy notice" lede="This site is built to know as little about you as possible. Here is exactly what happens when you visit it." />

  <div class="container privacy dim">
    <nav class="privacy__toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="label">Contents</p>
      <ol class="toc">
        {
          contents.map(([id, label]) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="summary">Summary</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No cookies, no analytics, no advertising, no tracking pixels, no fingerprinting, no session recording. One optional browser-storage entry if you use the light/dark toggle (see below).</li>
        <li>No contact form, no comment system, no embedded social-media widgets, no third-party fonts or scripts.</li>
        <li>The only data processing that happens when you visit is the hosting provider's own server logging (below).</li>
        <li>If you email me, I use your address and message to reply, and for nothing else.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="owner">Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        This website is published by {site.name}, a researcher based in the Netherlands, in a personal and
        professional capacity. It is not a business and offers nothing for sale. For anything concerning your
        personal data on this site, contact me at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="hosting">Hosting and server logs</h2>
      <p>
        The site is a set of static files served by <strong>GitHub Pages</strong>, a service of GitHub, Inc. (San
        Francisco, USA) and, for users in the EU, GitHub B.V. (Amsterdam). According to GitHub's documentation, when
        a GitHub Pages site is visited, the visitor's IP address is logged and stored by GitHub for security
        purposes, whether or not the visitor is signed in to GitHub. GitHub performs this logging for its own
        purposes under its own privacy statement; I do not receive, see or control these logs, and GitHub does not
        publish a retention period for them. GitHub states that it relies on EU standard contractual clauses and
        its certification under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework for transfers of personal data to the United
        States.
      </p>
      <p>
        Details: <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages#data-collection" rel="noopener">GitHub Pages data collection</a> and the <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        To the extent that I am regarded as a controller for this processing, the legal basis is legitimate interest
        (GDPR Article 6(1)(f)): running a professional website on infrastructure that is kept secure. No other data is
        collected on my behalf.
      </p>

      <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and local storage</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets <strong>no cookies</strong> and does not use session storage or IndexedDB. It loads no
        third-party scripts, fonts, images or embeds; all requests go to this site's own domain.
      </p>
      <p>
        The colour scheme follows your operating-system preference. If you use the sun/moon button in the header to
        choose the other scheme, that choice is kept in your browser's local storage under a single entry named
        <code>theme</code>, which records only the scheme name and the time you chose it. It is stored only while
        your choice differs from your system setting (switching back removes it), it expires after 180 days, it
        contains nothing that identifies you, and it never leaves your browser. Nothing else is stored, and nothing
        is stored at all unless you use that button. Because this is a preference you set yourself, no consent
        banner is shown.
      </p>
      <p>
        This was verified on the deployed site in a clean browser profile (see the <a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/COMPLIANCE_NOTES.md`} rel="noopener">compliance notes</a> in the source repository). If that ever changes, this notice will be updated first.
      </p>

      <h2 id="email">If you email me</h2>
      <p>
        The contact link opens your own email program. When you write to me I receive your email address, anything
        you include in the message, and the technical headers your mail provider adds. I use these to reply and to
        keep track of our correspondence, on the basis of your request (GDPR Article 6(1)(b)) or my legitimate
        interest in answering professional enquiries (Article 6(1)(f)). Messages are kept as long as the
        correspondence is relevant and then deleted. My mailbox is provided by Google (Gmail); Google's own privacy
        terms apply to the transport and storage of mail.
      </p>

      <h2 id="links">External links</h2>
      <p>
        The site links to external services: GitHub, ORCID, Google Scholar, ResearchGate, the University of
        Groningen research portal, DOI resolvers and publishers. These are ordinary links, not embeds; nothing is
        loaded from them until you choose to follow one. Their privacy policies apply once you leave this site.
      </p>

      <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the GDPR you have the right to access, rectify or erase personal data concerning you, to restrict or
        object to its processing, and to data portability where applicable. In practice the only personal data I hold
        about visitors is email correspondence, which I will show you, correct or delete on request. You also have the
        right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority; in the Netherlands this is the{' '}
        <a href="https://www.autoriteitpersoonsgegevens.nl/en" rel="noopener">Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens</a>.
        For server logs held by GitHub, please contact GitHub directly through its privacy statement.
      </p>

      <h2 id="content">Content and copyright</h2>
      <p>
        Text, page design and original graphics on this site (including the network figure on the home page and the
        project drawings) are © {site.name}. Reuse requires permission unless otherwise stated. The portrait
        photograph remains the copyright of its photographer and is used only on this site. Publications linked from this site
        belong to their publishers and authors and carry their own licences (most are CC BY 4.0, as marked). The
        fonts are Google Sans Flex and JetBrains Mono, used under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. A full provenance list is in the{' '}
        <a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/ASSET_PROVENANCE.md`} rel="noopener">source repository</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
      <p>
        This notice describes what the site does today. If the site's behaviour changes, the notice is revised before
        the change goes live. Last revised: <time datetime={site.privacyRevised}>{site.privacyRevised}</time>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6) var(--space-7);
    padding-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-8);
  }
  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .privacy {
      grid-template-columns: var(--margin-col) minmax(0, 1fr);
      padding-block: var(--space-7) var(--space-9);
    }
    .privacy__toc {
      position: sticky;
      top: 5.25rem;
      align-self: start;
    }
  }
  /* The contents list numbers itself the same way the headings do. */
  .toc {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    counter-reset: toc;
  }
  .toc li {
    max-width: none;
    counter-increment: toc;
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.6em;
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .toc li::before {
    content: counter(toc, decimal-leading-zero);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--ann-s);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--accent);
    flex: none;
    padding-top: 0.15em;
  }
  .toc a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 2.25rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .toc a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
